(Ooonana OS 0.9.4 field guide) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What it is) Tj
T*
(Ooonana OS is a scratch-built Linux project with its own rootfs, boot flow, installer) Tj
T*
(experiments, WSL export, and custom ooonana package manager.) Tj
T*
(Debian or Ubuntu are host build tools only. Alpine APKs are imported into Ooonana .pkg) Tj
T*
(repos; the target OS installs Ooonana packages, not live Alpine APKs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Editions) Tj
T*
(minimal: BusyBox-style rootfs, kernel, GRUB disk, installer ISO, WSL rootfs, command) Tj
T*
(line AI.) Tj
T*
(full-i3: minimal plus i3, Xorg, Spotlight-style launcher, movable GTK apps, wallpaper,) Tj
T*
(GUI installer, AI desktop app, and full WSL rootfs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Package install) Tj
T*
(ooonana update) Tj
T*
(ooonana search nano) Tj
T*
(ooonana show nano) Tj
T*
(ooonana get nano --dry-run) Tj
T*
(ooonana get nano) Tj
T*
(ooonana files nano) Tj
T*
(ooonana verify nano) Tj
T*
(ooonana upgrade) Tj
T*
(ooonana remove nano) Tj
T*
(ooonana purge nano) Tj
T*
(ooonana fix nano --reinstall) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Cloud repo) Tj
T*
(Default cloud path is the GitLab Pages direct repository:) Tj
T*
(https://ooonana.gitlab.io/ooonana-repo) Tj
T*
(Run ooonana update && ooonana upgrade. Metadata syncs first; package archives download) Tj
T*
(only when install or upgrade needs them.) Tj
T*
(GitHub Releases remains a backup tarball repository path.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Installer) Tj
T*
(Full-i3 live ISO boots i3. Installer requires explicit target and dry-run preview.) Tj
T*
(Erase-disk mode offers optional swap; custom root, home, swap and EFI must share) Tj
T*
(target disk.) Tj
